  "probe": "r-fix-wire-ado/batch-scope-group-unposted-edit",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-ADO-1",
    "ADO-BATCH-SCOPE",
    "ADO-VIEW"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-ado-1b/batch-scope-group: both adAffectGroup attempts failed while a row 3 edit was pending and with a string Filter, so the two causes were not separated. This probe has the pending edit and no string Filter. On a client static batch-optimistic recordset of SELECT ID, Code, V, V2, S FROM W ORDER BY ID (read-write copy of r-ado-1b-main): S of rows 1 and 2 set to \"g1\" and \"g2\" and posted with Update, S of row 3 set to \"g3\" with the edit left pending (EditMode read), Errors read and cleared; UpdateBatch(adAffectGroup) with no Filter (Errors right after); Filter = adFilterPendingRecords (EditMode, RecordCount, Errors) and UpdateBatch(adAffectGroup) (Errors right after); then Update on row 3, EditMode, and UpdateBatch(adAffectGroup) once more (Errors); the stored rows through Execute. Asks whether an unposted current edit blocks or joins a group submission.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
